{"id": "EUVD-2026-104307", "enisaUuid": "4ddf5184-3280-37f9-a60d-0aeff550794c", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.22 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows API clients to abort other users' in-flight generation requests by supplying a short client-controlled rid. Attackers can submit streaming /generate requests with single hex character rids and disconnect, triggering prefix-matching abort logic that terminates all other clients' requests.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T14:21:40", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45002", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/41474", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py#L5458-L5590", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L2425-L2436", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py#L2240-L2256", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.22-cross-request-abort-via-rid-prefix-matching"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112266", "GHSA-8v54-r9x8-p94v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac119a4a-1321-36bd-9d5d-fd2862dd57a0", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "464f2117-cea7-3bb4-a81b-a7697011aa1a", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}